== Biological Overview
The giraffe (_Giraffa camelopardalis_) is an African ruminant mammal.

- *Height:* Can reach up to 5.5 meters (18 feet).
- *Diet:* Primarily herbivorous, browsing on acacia leaves.
- *Heart:* Has a massive heart (up to 11kg) to pump blood up the long neck.

#pause



== Behavioral Characteristics 
Giraffes have evolved unique social and survival traits.

- *Social Structure:* Live in loose "towers" or groups.
- *Sleeping Habits:* Only require 5 to 30 minutes of sleep in a 24-hour period.
- *Defense:* A single kick from a giraffe can be fatal to a lion. #pause

